# Falcon-1024 public keys that `ttsnap fetch` checks snapshots against, one per line:
#
#   <name> <role> <base64 public key>
#
# A producer key signs the manifests of the snapshots it publishes; `ttsnap fetch` installs only a
# manifest signed by one. An attester key signs statements about the history its own node built;
# `ttsnap fetch -min-attest N` requires N of them to have signed the snapshot's statement.
# `ttsnap keygen -o <key file> -name <name> -role producer|attester` makes a key and prints its line.
#
# A private key stays on its host. To retire a key, remove its line (and ship a package update); to
# trust keys of your own, pass `ttsnap fetch -keys <your file>` instead of editing this one.

